Sampling \eqref{eq:orbit} at $t=mT_s$ yields the exact recurrence

\begin{equation}
\bm r_s[m+1]
=
2c_o\bm r_s[m]-\bm r_s[m-1],
\qquad
c_o\triangleq\cos(\omega_oT_s).
\label{eq:ar2}
\end{equation}

Let $\overline{\bm J}_\theta(\bm\theta)$ denote the normalized
Jacobian at $\bm\xi^+[m]$, and assume it is $\beta$-Lipschitz, i.e.,

\begin{equation}
\left\lVert 
\overline{\bm J}_\theta(\bm\theta_1)
-
\overline{\bm J}_\theta(\bm\theta_2)
\right\rVert_2
\leq
\beta\left\lVert \bm\theta_1-\bm\theta_2\right\rVert_2 ,
\label{eq:lipschitz}
\end{equation}

for all $\bm\theta_1,\bm\theta_2$ on the segment between $\bm\theta[m]$
and $\bm\theta[m]+\Delta\bm\theta^\star[m]$. Then

\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&
\left\lVert 
\overline{\bm\Gamma}
(\bm\xi^+;\bm\theta+\Delta\bm\theta^\star)
-\bm 1_K
\right\rVert_2
\\
&\leq
\eta
\left\lVert 
\left[
\overline{\bm J}_\theta^+
(\overline{\bm J}_\theta^+)^T
+\eta\bm I_K
\right]^{-1}
\overline{\bm b}
\right\rVert_2
+
\frac{\beta}{2}
\left\lVert \Delta\bm\theta^\star\right\rVert_2^2 .
\end{split}
\label{eq:error-bound}
\end{equation}
